# Frontend Rules

## Purpose
Keep the web app within the 4-layer UI model and prevent page-level styling drift.

## Scope
`apps/web` page, feature, and shared UI code.

## Hard Constraints
- MUST import UI primitives only from `@charts-gen/ui`.
- MUST NOT import design-system subpaths or define new UI primitives in app code.
- MUST NOT use `style={{}}`, CSS modules, or Tailwind utility strings in `app/` or `features/`.
- MUST use a named pattern for page layout.
- MUST wrap async data states with `<StateShell>`.
- MUST use `t()` for user-visible strings.

## Best Practices
- SHOULD keep pages style-free and delegate composition to patterns.

## Enforceability
- Lint: restricted imports, inline-style ban, and string-literal checks.
- CI: page-level style scan.
- Review: verify every page composes patterns instead of raw layout divs.

## Examples
### ✅ Valid
```tsx
<AppLayout sidebar={<ChartHistorySidebar />}>
  <SplitLayout top={<ChartCanvas />} bottom={<ChatInputPattern onSend={send} />} />
</AppLayout>
```

### ❌ Invalid
```tsx
<div style={{ display: 'flex', gap: 16 }} className="p-4">
  Save
</div>
```
